// One color channel, linearly interpolated from `core` (frac=0, the
// galaxy's center) to `edge` (frac=1000, its rim), with a small PRNG wobble
// (noise_range) so particles at the same radius aren't all identically
// colored, then clamped back into a byte (util.id).

tint_channel(int frac, int core, int edge) {
  int v = core + (edge - core) * frac / 1000;
  int j = noise_range(20);
} return int clamp255(v + j);
